<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM3-GUARD-SCOPE-GAP>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM3-GUARD-SCOPE-GAP" ;
  triage:title "The local-listener deletion guard enumerates 4 specific paths instead of asserting directory/workspace-wide absence, which is exactly how AM3-ACCEPT-LOOP-LEFTOVER went undetected" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-architecture/tests/boundary_enforcement.rs::ai11_deletion_gate_rejects_retired_windows_transport_ast_and_dependencies checks a hand-maintained 4-item array (local_tcp_transport.rs, local_ipc_transport.rs, local_ipc_connection.rs, local_ipc_transport/request_worker.rs) for file-existence, plus a substring check against exactly one file (lib.rs) for the module-name strings. It does not assert the local_ipc_transport/ directory as a whole is absent, and does not sweep the workspace the way its sibling AI.11 Windows-transport-identifier check does (via ai11_guarded_workspace_sources). The AM.1 Python guard (scripts/phase-am/check_legacy_transport_removal.py) has no local-listener category at all -- only raw-framing, peer-ingress, resend-replay, direct-sqlite, and daemon-harness. This gap is already named as the ledger's own open item AM-PLAN-007 ('make the guard contract match its stated scope') and was not closed by AM.3. Independently confirmed by arch-qa, ruthless-boundary-qa, and req-qa in the same QA-1 round." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "lint-gap" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
